# Workbooks — build, run & host your whole software stack

Workbooks is your whole software stack in one place — build apps, run AI agents, and host sites with your team. No servers to manage, no per-seat billing.

The heading above is the page `<title>` and this first paragraph is the meta/Open Graph description
(set by `Nexus.SSR.seo_meta`) — keep both as SEO-friendly product copy, since they're what search and
social previews show. The lander renders in app mode (its sections are `client` islands), so none of
this prose appears on the page itself; it exists to set the document head and to document the site.

## How the lander is built (dev notes — not rendered)

Our public landing page is a **folder of `.work` sections** — each its own file with the reasoning in
prose and the UI in a `client` block. The nexus composes them into one page; the shared look lives in
`design.work`; the behavior in `99-scripts.work`; brand assets (fonts, icons) travel with the workbook
as static files. It's one surface on our nexus, served at `/` via the deploy `home="lander"` knob,
alongside docs/cloud/waitlist/marketing.

## The sections

- **01-hero** — the promise + CTAs, over the lattice animation.
- **02-platforms** — build on desktop, ship to cloud.
- **03-cloud-pricing** — we don't bill per seat; we give you a machine.
- **03-cloud-tiers** — the offer: pick a machine + storage, no free tier ($20 floor).
- **04-what-is-a-workbook** — the atom of a living internet.
- **05-s3** — the closing build.
- **06-modal** — notify-me, captured into our waitlist workbook.

This workbook IS the live homepage (served at `/` via `home="lander"`); the old `web/index.html` god-file is retired.
